{
  "id": "defect-theory",
  "term": "defect theory",
  "definition": "In this context, defect theory refers to the view that pituitary stalk interruption syndrome may arise from congenital genetic abnormalities rather than delivery-related injury alone. It suggests that a person’s genetic background or specific gene mutations may disrupt normal embryonic development and contribute to the syndrome’s later clinical differences.",
